  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed rear roof dormer, by reason of its size, bulk, scale and massing and high level of visibility from the public street,&amp;nbsp; would\r\nresult in an overly dominant, incongruous, bulky and visually obtrusive form of\r\ndevelopment, which would be at odds with the prevailing visual character of\r\nboth the host property and wider area. The proposal is therefore contrary to\r\nthe high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2024), Policy D3.D1 and D3.D11 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of\r\nthe Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
